    <baseline value="0" year="2019"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual value="218">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="NL">From INERELA: The number is lower than in previous years as SWs who attended or received psycho-social support through official INERELA channels are now (informally) providing support to other sex workers. This a) reduces the need for SWs to approach INERELA, and b) is difficult to monitor or capture data via formal processes.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-30"></period-end>
     <actual value="2223">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="NL">Young people under the age of 24 find it difficult to open up to Religious Leaders about sex work as it is seen as taboo and acceptable behaviour in the society. The unclear legal status, criminalisation and discrimination of sex workers in these countries affects the number of sex workers who are willing to access psychological services, this number could have been more. Male are usually shy to come  out in the open and Cultural norms inhibit men from coming out. Zimbabwe Country Network had a challenge of assuming gays to be transgender and recorded under transgender. After discusion with the project officer he indicated that they were 6 male gays. So the number was incorporated under male until 24 years to make it 30.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
